## Context

`parseRef` in `tickets/tools/go/ticket.go` handles local refs, deprecated
schemes, case-variant old schemes, and forge refs, but has no dedicated
table test covering all paths.

## Actions

Add `TestParseRef` table-driven test in `ticket_test.go` with cases for:
- empty ref
- valid local refs (4 ASCII digits)
- non-4-digit / non-digit inputs
- deprecated gh: and gh# schemes
- case-variant old schemes (GH#, Gh:)
- valid forge refs (github.com, gitlab.com)
- invalid forge refs (leading zero, empty number, empty owner, wrong parts, colon in host)

## Exit criteria

- `go test -run TestParseRef -v` passes
- `make test` passes
- Tests are non-tautological (each case fails if parseRef logic changes)
